WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:14.706
Unit twenty-four: Let's (suggestions). Today you will make suggestions and agree with ideas.

4
00:00:15.006 --> 00:00:17.612
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.707
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.377
Let's.

7
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:27.683
Let's means short for let us, used to make a suggestion.

8
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:29.702
Let's play football.

9
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:32.992
Your turn. Say: Let's.

10
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:36.672
Let's.

11
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.569
Suggestion.

12
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:42.535
Suggestion means an idea that you offer to someone.

13
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.766
That is a good suggestion.

14
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.107
Your turn. Say: Suggestion.

15
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.142
Suggestion.

16
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:53.664
Go.

17
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.766
Go means to move to another place.

18
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.641
Let's go to the park.

19
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.415
Your turn. Say: Go.

20
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.047
Go.

21
00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:06.564
Play.

22
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.584
Play means to do something for fun.

23
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.626
Let's play a game.

24
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:14.254
Your turn. Say: Play.

25
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:17.718
Play.

26
00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:19.101
Eat.

27
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.186
Eat means to put food in your mouth.

28
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:23.959
Let's eat lunch.

29
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.599
Your turn. Say: Eat.

30
00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:30.179
Eat.

31
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:31.744
Watch.

32
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.168
Watch means to look at something for a time.

33
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:37.040
Let's watch a film.

34
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.966
Your turn. Say: Watch.

35
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.615
Watch.

36
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.525
Good idea.

37
00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:49.352
Good idea means a reply to agree with a suggestion.

38
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.266
Good idea! Let's do it.

39
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.433
Your turn. Say: Good idea.

40
00:01:58.267 --> 00:01:59.198
Good idea.

41
00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:00.916
Why not.

42
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.659
Why not means a reply to say yes to a suggestion.

43
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.542
Why not? It sounds fun.

44
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.686
Your turn. Say: Why not.

45
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.546
Why not.

46
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:18.891
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.332
Visal, it is Saturday. What do you want to do? Make a suggestion.

48
00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:35.203
Let's go to the park! We use let's and the base verb to suggest an activity: Let's play football. Let's watch a film. Let's eat together.

49
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:38.247
How can the other person reply?

50
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:51.788
To agree, we can say: Good idea! Why not? Okay. To say no politely: Sorry, I can't. Maybe another time. Let's is friendly and invites us.

51
00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:54.813
How do we make a negative suggestion?

52
00:02:55.917 --> 00:03:06.617
We say Let's not: Let's not be late. It is a gentle way to say we should not do something. A question is also possible: Why don't we go?

53
00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.197
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.721
Grammar focus: Suggestions: Let's plus base verb.

55
00:03:14.021 --> 00:03:15.208
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:17.359
Let's go to the park.

57
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.041
Let's watch a film tonight.

58
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.950
Let's not be late for class.

59
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:31.974
Use Let's + base verb to suggest an activity and Let's not + base verb for a negative suggestion. Reply with Good idea or Why not.

60
00:03:32.717 --> 00:03:35.590
Be careful! Don't say: Let's to go home.

61
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:39.080
Say: Let's go home.

62
00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.298
Use the base verb after let's.

63
00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.194
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.431
Making Plans.

65
00:03:47.731 --> 00:03:50.090
It is Saturday, so let's go to the park.

66
00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.819
Let's play football and then eat lunch together.

67
00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.776
Good idea! Why not invite our friends too?

68
00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.569
Let's watch a film in the evening.

69
00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.669
Let's not be late, because the bus leaves at nine.

70
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:09.943
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.110
blank play football!

72
00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.680
A, Lets. B, Let's. C, Let.

73
00:04:19.233 --> 00:04:21.175
The answer is B: Let's.

74
00:04:22.317 --> 00:04:23.747
Let's blank to the market.

75
00:04:24.047 --> 00:04:27.527
A, go. B, going. C, goes.

76
00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.322
The answer is A: go.

77
00:04:34.483 --> 00:04:36.924
A good reply to a suggestion is blank.

78
00:04:37.224 --> 00:04:41.609
A, Good idea!. B, Good bye!. C, Good night!.

79
00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.271
The answer is A: Good idea!.

80
00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:49.975
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.275 --> 00:04:54.880
A, Let's to play now.. B, Let's play now.. C, Let's playing now..

82
00:04:58.433 --> 00:05:00.700
The answer is B: Let's play now..

83
00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.790
According to the reading, why should we not be late?

84
00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:10.055
A, the bus leaves at nine. B, it is Saturday. C, the film is long.

85
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.424
The answer is A: the bus leaves at nine.

86
00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:20.808
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.544
Make a suggestion for this weekend using 'Let's'.

88
00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.966
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:35.266 --> 00:05:47.781
Let's go to the river on Sunday morning and have a picnic. We can eat rice and fruit and play games. I use let's and the base verb to make the suggestion. My friends can answer, Good idea!

90
00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.686
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:55.813
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and suggestions: let's plus base verb.

92
00:05:56.113 --> 00:05:59.961
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

93
00:06:00.261 --> 00:06:03.285
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:05.982
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

